module

public import ECA.Basic

/-!
# Rule `110`'s window column families

Data for the column families of rule `110`: the six purely periodic families of the
window read from the leftmost set cell, each as one 64-bit word per column, bit `n`
the cell's value at step `n`, tabulated up to its shift-symmetric tail. A tail triple
`(S, τ, j₀)` says that from column `j₀` on column `j + S` at step `n` is column `j` at
step `n + τ`. A sibling triple `(j, k, τ)` says that family `k` read `τ` steps later
agrees with this family below column `j` and is its complement at column `j`. The
encoding is stated at the theorems that consume these lists; this file is data and
proves nothing.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace ECA

